content.text:
Now update updateMenuScene. Current lines 1023-1035. Replace dog part.

Plan:
```
const cyc = (t + 3) % 27;
let targetX=0.04, targetRot=-0.52, walking=0, sniffing=0, alerting=0;
if (cyc < 6.5) { targetX=.58; targetRot=.12; walking=1; }
else if (cyc < 9.0) { targetX=.58; targetRot=.04; alerting=1; }
else if (cyc < 15.5) { targetX=-.58; targetRot=Math.PI-.12; walking=1; }
else if (cyc < 18.0) { targetX=-.58; targetRot=Math.PI-.28; sniffing=1; }
else { targetX=.04; targetRot=-.52; }
menuDogPose.x = lerp(... 1-exp(-dt*1.4)); rot...
menuDog.position.x = menuDogPose.x;
menuDog.rotation.y = menuDogPose.rot + sin...
// avoid clipping platform? no
menuDog.userData.targetLook = walking ? .03 : (menuPointerX || Math.sin(t*.23)*.12);
menuDog.userData.update(dt,t,{baseY:.3,audioBark:!hidden && t>8,gait:walking,sniff:sniffing,alert:alerting});
```
But if walking left (rot π-.12), targetLook positive might rotate head beyond. Fine.

Actually when cyc 18-27 idle, targetX .04 rot -.52. At t=0 (cyc 3) walking right starting from x .04; fine.

But moving targetX .58 over 6.5s is only .08/s, slow. The dog doesn't need to cover ground fast. Walking gait at t*9.5 while moving slowly looks like marching in place. Better set speed based on distance. Instead use lerp rate 1.6: x reaches target in ~1.5s and then remains while gait continues. Could set target based on cycle and walk slower: use `menuDogPose.x += clamp(targetX - x, -1,1) * dt * .38` -> .38 u/s, 1.5s to cross .58. Then still walks in place for rest. Hmm.

Better make targetX follow cycle continuously:
- Right walk segment 0-6.5: targetX = -0.35 + (cyc/6.5)*0.9 (~ -0.35 -> .55) and walking=1.
- left walk 9-15.5: targetX = .55 - ((cyc-9)/6.5)*.9.
- idle target holds at ends.
At 0.14 u/s, foot gait at 9.5 rad/s would be too fast. The dog's gait cycle at 9.5 rad/s means ~1.5 steps/s; stride maybe .3 units → .45 u/s, closer. Dog is small scale .94; moving .9 units/6.5 = .14 u/s is slow, so feet slide a bit, but acceptable for a guard dog pacing.

Maybe don't patrol; keep dog centered and do a "turn in place" at intervals. Hmm.

Human viewers won't scrutinize foot-slide. The motion will make menu feel alive. Keep simple lerp.

Use `targetX` .50/- .50. At right end, rot 0.04, alert; at left end rot π-.12, sniff. Good.

Let's patch.

